Model inputs, numerical results, and manuscript
----------------------------------------------

Third-party model inputs retain their own terms. The software GPL notice does
not replace those terms or license the separately distributed manuscript.
PREM model tables and adapted model inputs are redistributed under CC BY 4.0
on the policy basis recorded below. They are distinguished from the recorded
Disper26 phase velocities, kernels, Hessians, tables, and reports.

* PREM source: the bundled model is the IRIS EMC anisotropic PREM table,
  now distributed by EarthScope as PREM_ANISOTROPIC_IDV.csv. The model page
  identifies this variant as the anisotropic PREM used by SAW24B16:
  https://data.earthscope.org/app/products/portal/emc_model_viewer.html?id=EMC-PREM
  Model-page DOI: https://doi.org/10.17611/DP/9991844 .
  Current source file:
  https://data.earthscope.org/archive/seismology/products/emc/data/PREM/PREM_ANISOTROPIC_IDV.csv

  Source verification on 2026-10-20 found that the bundled file differs only
  by its name and one additional final LF newline. All 97 data rows and nine
  columns, including their units and numerical values, are unchanged.
  The upstream file is 6556 bytes; SHA-256:
  dd70ea9074b586b7182cc0c04b3e21ef762dd27dddd610a9843d896b10d31fb3.
  The bundled file is 6557 bytes; SHA-256:
  fd602a8b6a985b2569df64113891c2ae5ee3ab57cf827ae0ab0927ff886a90b7.
  disper26/data/model_PREM_aniso.csv, tests/model_PREM_aniso.csv, and the
  copies listed in the frozen source manifests are byte-identical.

  Model credit: Dziewonski, A. M., and Anderson, D. L. (1981),
  Preliminary reference Earth model, Physics of the Earth and Planetary
  Interiors, 25, 297-356, https://doi.org/10.1016/0031-9201(81)90046-7 .
  EarthScope/IRIS data-products credit: Trabant, C., Hutko, A. R., Bahavar, M.,
  Karstens, R., Ahern, T., and Aster, R. (2012), Data Products at the IRIS DMC:
  Stepping Stones for Research and Other Applications, Seismological Research
  Letters, 83(5), 846-854, https://doi.org/10.1785/0220120032 .

* PREM terms: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0):
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ .
  The basis is EarthScope's facility data policy, effective 2025-06-12:
  https://resess.unavco.org/data/policies_forms/data-policy/data-license.html .
  That policy assigns CC BY 4.0 by default where a contributing provider has
  not specified a more restrictive license; existing more restrictive terms
  take precedence. No separate restrictive term was found in the model record
  or CSV reviewed on 2026-10-20. On that basis, the PREM tables and adapted
  model inputs here are redistributed under CC BY 4.0. Preserve source and
  model credits, links to the data and license, and descriptions of changes.

* Adapted PREM inputs: tests/fixtures/prem_tracking_model.json contains solid
  model nodes after unit conversion and earth flattening, for Disper26-only
  tracking regressions. It contains no external-program reference output.
  The PREM source credit and CC BY 4.0 terms above also cover these adapted
  model inputs. The CSV itself remains in its original SI units; unit
  conversion, ocean handling, depth selection, interpolation, and optional
  earth flattening are performed by the model loaders, as documented in
  disper26/_prem.py and inversion/disper26_inv/prem.py.

* Recorded Disper26 results: paper/data/ contains fixed numerical arrays and
  reports from Disper26 calculations. Their historical calculation sources
  and content fingerprints are recorded in paper/reference_manifest.json and
  paper/data/results/provenance.json. These calculations are distinct from
  external-program reference output. Preserve the PREM attribution above for
  PREM-derived model inputs stored with those results.

The paper/README.md, paper/reference_manifest.json, and
paper/data/results/provenance.json describe the historical source snapshots
and numerical evidence. Historical snapshots preserve their original
third-party license files. External-program comparison tests, output, and
benchmark reports are outside this distribution.

